# 2025-11-24 14:16:22.005408
+FUZZY ANSWER PROCESSING
+When validating the user answer you must apply flexible logic
+1 Case Insensitivity Treat water Water and WATER as identical.
+2 Subscript Tolerance Treat standard text numbers as subscripts. Example CO2 matches $CO_2$ and h2so4 matches $H_2SO_4$.
+3 Format Flexibility Accept both the Name and the Formula unless the question explicitly forbids one. Example if the answer is Sodium Chloride accept NaCl as correct.
+4 Spacing Ignore extra spaces or commas in lists. Example 1 2 1 is the same as 1,2,1.
+1. No More "Case Sensitive" ErrorsBefore: If you typed "hcl" but the answer was "HCl", the AI would say "Wrong".Now: The AI is instructed to ignore capitalization.Input: nacl, NACL, or NaCl → ALL CORRECT.2. "Big Numbers" are Okay (Subscript Tolerance)Before: You had to know how to format small numbers (subscripts) which is hard to type on a phone.Now: The AI treats regular text numbers as chemical subscripts.Input: H2SO4 (standard text) → Read as: $H_2SO_4$ (Correct).3. Interchangeable Answers (Abbreviation)Before: If the question asked "Name this" and you typed the formula, it might fail.Now: It accepts both the Name and the Formula unless specifically told otherwise.Question: "What is Table Salt?"Input: Sodium Chloride OR NaCl → BOTH CORRECT.4. Spacing ForgivenessNow: It doesn't care if you use commas or spaces for balancing equations.Input: 1, 2, 1 OR 1 2 1 → BOTH CORRECT.Getty ImagesExploreThis makes the "mini-app" feel much smarter and less frustrating to play!
+

